) (so \\(a+b\\le n\\)), then \\((a,b)\\) belongs to the line\n     \\(L_{b}\\) because substituting \\(x=a\\) in \\(L_{b}\\) yields  \n\n     \\[\n     y=\\frac{n+1-b}{b}\\,a=n+1-b-\\frac{a-b}{b}=b .\n     \\]\n\n     Hence every required lattice point belongs to one of the \\(n\\) lines\n     \\(\\{L_{1},\\dots ,L_{n}\\}\\).  All \\(n\\) lines are sunny, giving exactly\n     \\(k=n\\) sunny lines.\n\nSince the three constructions work and Lemma 1 shows that no other value of\n\\(k\\) is possible, the set of admissible \\(k\\) is precisely \\(\\{0,1,n\\}\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{All admissible }k\\text{ are }k=0,\\;k=1,\\;k=n.}\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
